{{draft}}
[[ja:大祓]]
{{AFC comment|Current redirect at [[Oharae]] is just wrong and shouldn't be there. [[Oharae no Kotoba]] is a component of this festival. [[Oharae]] should redirect here instead. [[User:Immanuelle|'''Immanuel'''le]] ❤️💚💙 [[User_talk:Immanuelle|(talk to the cutest Wikipedian)]] 19:48, 5 June 2023 (UTC)}}
[[{{PAGENAME}}]] is a Shinto ritual also known as the Great Purification<ref>https://www.senninso.com/oharae-thegreatpurification/</ref> It is hosted annually on June 30th.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nagoshi no Oharae Purification Ritual |url=https://www.kamigamojinja.jp/en/rituals/nagoshi-no-oharae-purification-ritual/ |access-date=2023-06-05 |website=Kamo Wakeikazuchi Jinja Shrine (Kamigamo Jinja) |language=ja}}</ref> It is also hosted on December 30th.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Meador |first=Spencer |date=2017-07-04 |title=Oharae |url=http://sanpai-japan.com/2017/07/04/oharae/ |access-date=2023-06-05 |website=Sanpai Japan |language=en-US}}</ref> The last one is sometimes done on New years eve instead.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Shiwasu Oharae-shiki (Great Purification Ceremony in December) {{!}} Samukawa-jinja Shrine |url=https://samukawajinjya.jp/en/festival/shiwasuoharae.html |access-date=2023-06-05 |website=Samukawa-jinja Shrine Official Website |language=en}}</ref>

It is also  done at [[Isonokami Shrine]]
{{Japanese Imperial Rituals}}

